        "title": "Your HomePod has a colorful new party trick: how to enable Sound Glow",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/19/homepod-sound-glow-colorful-light/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/10/homepod-sound-glow.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple is rolling out a new feature for <a href=\"https://apple.sjv.io/jR3VPn\">HomePod mini</a> and the second-gen<a href=\"https://apple.sjv.io/enMaDg\"> big HomePod</a> called Sound Glow. This lights up the touch surface of your speaker with colors that reference the album artwork of the currently playing song, perhaps adding some additional ambience to a party vibe.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s how to enable the new Sound Glow feature …</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"apple-tv,homepod\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1074852\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/19/homepod-sound-glow-colorful-light/#more-1074852\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
