        "title": "Apple SVP Greg Joswiak: ‘We don’t feel threatened’ by OpenAI hardware plans",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/15/apple-svp-greg-joswiak-we-dont-feel-threatened-by-openai-hardware-plans/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/10/greg-joz-joswiak-event-sep-2026-1.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Today in a <a href=\"https://time.com/collection/best-inventions/2026/apple-iphone-duo/\">new story at <em>TIME</em></a>, the publication <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/15/john-ternus-talks-iphone-duo-cheap-and-crappy-foldables-in-new-interview/\">interviewed CEO John Ternus</a> but also spoke to Greg “Joz” Joswiak, Apple’s SVP of Worldwide Marketing, who addressed the “lunatic fringe” of AI in Silicon Valley, hardware threats from OpenAI, and more.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"greg-joswiak,openai\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1074334\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/15/apple-svp-greg-joswiak-we-dont-feel-threatened-by-openai-hardware-plans/#more-1074334\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
